# **4. Business Model Architecture**

| **Layer** | **Product** | **Purpose** | **Revenue Role** | **When to Invest** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1** | **Managed AI Operations** | Core service — configure, manage, and improve AI workflows for SMB clients | Primary — onboarding + retainer | Day 1 |
| **2** | **Private AI Infrastructure** | Premium capability for clients with confidentiality, compliance, or privacy needs | Add-on margin enhancer | Month 4–6, demand-triggered |
| **3** | **Vertical Free Tools** | Lead magnets and trust builders — one per target vertical | Lead generation, not revenue | Month 1–2, pre-outreach |
| **4** | **Long-Term Platform** | Client portal, monitoring dashboard, vertical app marketplace, AI Ops control plane | Scalability and LTV expansion | Year 2+, post-playbook validation |

 

## **Layer 1 — Managed AI Operations (Core Business)**

The company helps SMBs identify AI-ready administrative workflows, automate them, integrate with existing software, train staff, and maintain the operations monthly. The company displaces manual admin labor, fragmented MSP digital ops, and poorly implemented internal AI experiments. The customer is not buying AI — they are buying operational execution and peace of mind.

Revenue is driven by onboarding fees (one-time setup) and managed retainers (recurring monthly). The retainer is the core economic engine.

 

## **Layer 2 — Private AI Infrastructure (Premium Differentiator)**

For clients with attorney-client privilege concerns, HIPAA-sensitive workflows, or confidential business data, Private AI Ops can deploy dedicated GPU inference endpoints, RAG pipelines, zero-retention architecture, per-client access controls, and audit-friendly logging. This infrastructure is not sold as commodity compute — it is sold as a managed private AI operating environment.

The residential GPU hosting PoC validates the technical architecture. Infrastructure should be deployed only when client demand justifies it, either because signed contracts pre-sell the capacity or because private infrastructure demonstrably improves close rates and gross margin.

 

## **Layer 3 — Vertical Free Tools (Distribution)**

Each vertical receives a purpose-built free tool that solves one narrow, high-visibility pain point. These tools collect qualified lead data, demonstrate domain knowledge, and route high-intent prospects into discovery calls. They are not the product — they are distribution mechanisms.

 

## **Layer 4 — Long-Term Platform (Year 2+)**

After services create repeatable patterns, the company can develop a managed AI control plane, client-facing portal, workflow monitoring, vertical app marketplace, and reusable SOP libraries. This is a Year 2 initiative. Do not build it before services create the pattern it should encode.

 

