| Discovery-to-proposal rate | > 60% | > 70% | < 40% |
| Proposal-to-close rate | > 30% | > 40% | < 20% |
| Onboarding revenue (total) | $7,000–15,000 | $60,000–120,000 | < $3,500 by Month 3 |
| Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR) | $3,000–6,000 | $15,000–25,000 | $0 by Month 4 |
| Active retainer clients | 2–3 | 6–10 | < 1 by Month 4 |
| Implementation hours per client onboarding | 30–50 hrs (learning curve) | 15–25 hrs (playbook) | > 70 hrs per client |
| Monthly support hours per retainer client | 10–15 hrs | 5–8 hrs (optimization) | > 20 hrs/client |
| Infrastructure attach rate | 0–1 clients | 20–30% of retainer clients | N/A (demand-triggered) |

 

## **Decision Gates**

| **Gate** | **Condition to Pass** | **Unlocks** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **G1 — Hardware Deployment** | 2+ infrastructure clients signed. ISP upgraded. Circuit installed. LLC formed. BAA ready. | 4-GPU build at 38 Chestnut proceeds |
| **G2 — Dental Vertical** | Law firm playbook documented. 2+ law firm retainers paying. Founder bandwidth confirmed. | Dedicated dental outreach begins |
| **G3 — Delivery Support Hire** | 3–4 retainer clients active. Monthly support hours exceeding 40+ hrs/week for founder. | Part-time technical implementation support hired |
| **G4 — Third Vertical** | Law + dental playbooks documented. Combined MRR > $10,000. Dedicated vertical lead available. | Property management or financial SMB vertical activated |
| **G5 — Colocation Migration** | 5+ infrastructure clients. Revenue target $5,000+/mo infrastructure add-on MRR. Residential power ceiling approached. | Miami/Doral colo evaluation and Phase 3 build planning |
| **G6 — Platform Development** | 10+ retainer clients. Onboarding playbooks for 2+ verticals documented. Combined MRR > $25,000. | Client portal, monitoring dashboard, and vertical app marketplace |

 

# **18. Final Strategic Recommendation**

| *Launch as a managed AI Ops services business. Use private infrastructure as a premium differentiator and future moat. Do not lead with residential GPU hosting. Validate paid workflow demand first, then deploy infrastructure only when it is pre-sold or clearly improves close rate and margin.* |
| --- |

 

| **Strategic Question** | **Decision** |
| --- | --- |
| **Should this launch as GPU hosting or AI Ops services?** | AI Ops services. GPU hosting is a capability, not the business. |
| **What should the first vertical be?** | Small law firms in South Florida. Heppner ruling creates urgent, real, and monetizable pain. |
| **What should be sold first?** | AI Ops Assessment ($1,500) converting to Managed AI Onboarding ($5,000–8,000) and a $2,000–3,000/month retainer. |
| **When should private infrastructure be introduced?** | Month 2–3 as a discovery call and demo asset. Deployed only when signed clients pre-sell the capacity. Never speculatively. |
| **What should be built in the first 90 days?** | LLC, contract templates, Law Brief free tool, landing page, prospect list, discovery call process, first onboarding playbook, first case study. |
| **What should be avoided?** | Buying hardware before signed clients. Launching three verticals simultaneously. Marketing as a GPU hosting business. Overclaiming compliance. Building software before services create the pattern. |

 

## **What This Business Is**

| **The Business Is** | **The Business Is Not** |
| --- | --- |
| A managed AI operations firm for privacy-sensitive SMBs | A residential GPU hosting company |
| A compliance-aware workflow automation provider | A raw compute marketplace competitor |
| A founder-led, relationship-driven local services business | A passive income or SaaS-first operation |
| A proof of concept for Miami-area colocation at Phase 3 | A fully compliant data center (do not represent it as one) |
| An embedded operational partner that deepens value every month | A consulting firm that advises and leaves |

 

## **Final Assessment**

The technical infrastructure is viable. The compliance architecture is achievable. The target market — South Florida privacy-sensitive SMBs, starting with law firms — is real, underserved, and actively looking for a solution to the Heppner and HIPAA exposure created by public AI tools. The financial model reaches $3,000–6,000/month MRR by Month 3 with two onboarding clients and breaks into five-figure MRR territory by Month 12 with a functioning retainer base.

The single largest risk is failing to close two managed AI Ops retainer clients before committing to infrastructure spend. That is a sales execution risk, not a technical risk. Solve the sales problem first. Buy the hardware second.

 

